WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.351
KALLAX can be used as one shelving unit
or combined into a larger storage system.

00:00:05.351 --> 00:00:09.843
Plan the layout first, whether it will
stand on the floor, mount to a wall,

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.400
or work as a room divider.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.200
Select the unit sizes that fit your space,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.664
then fully assemble every KALLAX unit
before positioning or combining them.

00:00:19.664 --> 00:00:23.950
The frames should be complete and
square before you stack or align them.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.196
Use the provided tip-over restraint
to secure the furniture to the wall.

00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:33.623
This is especially important when units
are stacked higher or arranged where they

00:00:33.623 --> 00:00:35.810
could tip, such as a room divider setup.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.602
Place the unit in an
orientation suited to the room.

00:00:40.602 --> 00:00:43.362
Use vertical placement for narrow spaces,

00:00:43.362 --> 00:00:47.268
horizontal placement for a low
sideboard or media console,

00:00:47.268 --> 00:00:50.500
and only use underframes
with compatible models.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:56.362
Before combining multiple units, make
sure the floor is completely level.

00:00:56.362 --> 00:01:01.401
An uneven base can make stacked units
unstable and stop the frames from lining up

00:01:01.401 --> 00:01:02.770
flush with each other.
